861:## Wave 017 — Three presentation read ports and realization boundary
939:## Wave 018 — Domain realization context boundary
943:Added by `cycle-018-wave-plan-extension` as the recommended next wave after Wave 017. Requires `cycle-018-wave-plan-extension-review` sign-off before the canonical `cycle-018-fresh-scout-proposals` stage and before any implementation.
1035:## Wave 019 — Three scene-host lifecycle and renderer platform boundary
1039:Added by `cycle-018-wave-plan-extension` correction as the recommended next ordered wave after Wave 018. Requires the Cycle 018 wave-plan-extension review to sign off the ordering before any Wave 019 scout/proposal or implementation. Wave 019 must be re-read after Wave 018 completes; if Wave 018 changes realization/read-context assumptions materially, update this entry through a reviewed plan-edit mini-cycle before implementation.
1060:If Wave 018 leaves full-`World` or `any` realization seams that still force renderer decisions to depend on domain internals, stop and run a reviewed plan edit before starting this wave. If implementation discovers user-facing 3D interaction behavior must change beyond encoding the existing lifecycle/ownership contract, cover it with focused e2e/live evidence or stop for a mini-cycle.
1064:The baseline identified 3D rendering concentration as a major residual rendering risk: `ThreeView.vue` originally combined scene setup, projection-plane rendering, 2D-on-3D rendering, 3D elements, guide geometry, hinge lines, animation, resize, cleanup, domain realization access, and store access (`architecture-audit/baseline/quality-report.md`, Q5; `architecture-audit/baseline/architecture-map.md`, “God-modules”; `architecture-audit/baseline/risk-register.md`, R8). Waves 016 and 017 narrowed the canvas/three presentation read-model boundary first, and Wave 018 is ordered ahead of this entry so the scene platform consumes typed realization/read outputs rather than preserving full-`World` realization seams.
1092:Depends on Wave 018 because scene-host lifecycle should consume stable typed realization/read-context outputs rather than compensate for domain realization contracts that still require full `World` or `any`. It is ordered before app-shell service concentration, backend/frontend contract stance, validation-gate hardening, placeholder/debug cleanup, and docs/spec drift because the remaining 3D runtime/platform boundary is still central user-visible architecture while those later topics either depend on stable rendering contracts or are more peripheral cleanup.
